Z||000000||Alex2004||06-01-2001||06:31 PM||||I got my Bulldog model 1402 keyless entry system today, so i installed it...  except when i lock/unlock it the doors don't do anything but the light's flash and the horn honks, so i started the car and pushed the button except this time the doors lock and unlock, so i shut it off again, and i pushed the button and it locks, but no unlock even though the lights flash, Does anyone know what i did wrong??? Here is what i wired, door lock/unlock, parking light, ground, and the constant power on the steering column, and the ingnition power on the steering column... I'm not through but i still think the door locks should work with car off... Let me know, thanks....<P>Alex...   <A HREF="mailto:AbercrombieAlex15@hotmail.com">AbercrombieAlex15@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||13
Z||000001||Oreif||06-01-2001||07:52 PM||||It sounds like you hooked the control line of the door locks to accessory power (Only has power when ignition is on) and you need to hook it to constant power. If you look at the drawing of how the alarm connects, Take a meter and see if all the wires that get constant 12VDC have it. Sometimes they call it battery when they mean constant 12VDC.<P>Just reread your post,<P>Does the alarm have a delayed dome light feature? If it does that would explain why after you started the car then turned it off the doors locked. The wire you are probably using is hooked to the dome light delay. Once the alarm arms itself it turns the dome light off. (no more power to unlock). Check the wiring again. Especially the lock control and dome light control.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Alex2004||06-01-2001||08:03 PM||||mine does have the delayed dome light option and i have the relay for it but i haven't installed it yet, i just want to get the locks to work first.  I checked the wires and they are right.  It says BLUE for lock and BLUE/white for unlock, i have them installed correct, oh my door's would lock when i shut it off w/ the remote, and would have unlocked once after i locked them, anymore ideas that might help, i called bulldog and they said it's either a bad constant or a bad ground, so i changed the ground and it's really good and i soldered the constant even more so it's a good constant, and i have my ignition power wired to the pink ignition wire. I'm confused right now but if you can help please let me know, thanks for your help...<P>Alex...||||reg||1
