Z||000004||grinthock||06-01-2001||10:04 PM||||Did you add those power door locks yourself?  Did you use a PDL Relay unit or build the relay circuit yourself?  I have been through ALL of what you are saying it's a ***** .||||reg||1
Z||000005||Oreif||06-01-2001||10:39 PM||||There should be a wire that you hook to either 12VDC or ground depending on the type of car. Some cars have a Negative trigger door lock and some have a positive trigger door lock. Aside from the wires you attached to the lock/unlock wires, There should also be a trigger wire or control wire. You probably have this wire either mis-wired or not connected.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Alex2004||06-02-2001||01:16 AM||||grinthock, these are factory Fiero locks and i didn't add them, they were there when i got the car, and i didn't need any relays for the locks, i even called Bulldog and asked them before i ordered it because i didn't want to mess w/ wiring relays.  I wired the lock/unlock wires on the drivers side, and then i re-did it and took the conecter off and soldered the lock/unlock wire into the factory lock unlock wire so it has a really good connection.  Orief, i also called Bulldog about what type of lock's Fiero's have and they are Type A which are positive trigger and i wired them correctly also from what the manual says and i have checked it so many times.  Earlier i was messing w/ it and i started the car to let it run and charge up the battery and say there and locked/unlocked away w/ the remote, and after i shut it off, it actually worked about 5 or 6 times then only the lock would work, right now i have lock working just fine, but it still won't unlock unless the car is running.  This is really confusing, ugh....well thanks for the help, hopfully you can figure out what i did wrong.  I'll go get the maunal and tell you exactly what i wired including colors ( alarm/Fiero) and i'll post that, and i'll even type some of what it says, and maybe you can tell me if you want mmkay... THANKS AGAIN  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Alex...<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Alex2004||06-02-2001||01:33 AM|||| the ( ) mean's Bulldog, * * means Fiero, (**)mean both color's same : Here is what i have wired so far, the Constant Power (*RED*) located at the steering column, GROUND (*BLACK*), which put a fisheye looking crimp thing and drilled a hole by the drivers kick panel into the fame, sanded the screw where it would touch the fish eye, sanded the metal where the screw goes to make a good ground, conected the ignition(YELLOW) *PINK* power at steering column, then i connected the parking light wire(*BROWN*) to the parking light. On Fiero the LT BLUE IS LOCK, AND BLACK IS UNLOCK, now here is what i did. (INSTRUCTION SAID) Connect the main wiring harness's <B>blue</B> wire to the wire marked lock (i had to label), then it said connect the main wiring harness's blue/white wire to the wire marked unlock.  so i connected blue w/lt.blue & blue/white w/black, and i soldered all of this to make a good connection, and that is all i have done so far except put the LED in, i haven't wired my door pin tigger for the alarm yet that senses when door is open to sound the alarm, or my dome light/relay yet either because once i am done wiring everything i just want to hide it and leave it alone.  Sorry that was so long, i am just hoping someone will think of a solution for this....hope this helps. Thanks for being patient and reading all of this...<P>Alex...<p>[This message has been edited by Alex2004 (edited 06-02-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||Oreif||06-02-2001||03:34 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Alex2004:<BR><B>  i haven't wired my door pin tigger for the alarm yet that senses when door is open to sound the alarm, or my dome light/relay yet either because once i am done wiring everything i just want to hide it and leave it alone.  Sorry that was so long, i am just hoping someone will think of a solution for this....hope this helps. Thanks for being patient and reading all of this...<P>Alex...<P>[This message has been edited by Alex2004 (edited 06-02-2001).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Alex, I went to Bulldog's site and looked at their installation guide. You need to hook up the door trigger! On page 6 of the guide I looked at says to "make sure you hook up the door triggers or the alarm won't arm and keyless entry will not work correctly"<P>Try hooking up the door trigger then see if it works. I bet what's happening is the alarm thinks the door is open so it never arms correctly. So it is waiting to arm and it won't unlock.<BR>If I rememeber it's the green/white wire of the alarm box.<P>Here is the link to the guide.<BR>Note: you need Adobe Acrobat Reader to view it.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.bulldogsecurity.com/pdf/Model1402.pdf" TARGET=_blank>http://www.bulldogsecurity.com/pdf/Model1402.pdf</A> <BR><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 06-02-2001).]||||reg||4
